 - [TADR-003 § Consequences](../../../adr/TADR-003-content-pipeline.md#consequences), line 41: TADR-004 stores content revisions and references, and a missing ID may not be silently remapped, a saved offer may not be rerolled and an old run may not be retired as a cleanup shortcut. This section cites that line directly for the no-remap rule rather than through any other record.
 - Bible [§ Runs, regions, exits and saves](../../../BIBLE.md#runs-regions-exits-and-saves), lines 576 to 586. Line 578 makes a world a run-region and leaves levels per world and the procedural technique open. Line 580 gives a world transition two randomly selected eligible destinations, independent of the number or format of item rewards. Line 582 gives one standard revival per run and leaves revival health, placement and unfinished-level interruption unresolved. Line 584 preserves the build and resolved rewards with resume at the next entrance, keeps already offered choices stable, forbids duplicating rewards, refilling a spent revival or resurrecting a terminal run, and says that pausing the dashboard is not itself a checkpoint. Line 586 carries permanent discoveries, learned recipes, options and challenges through defeat while the next run rebuilds equipment power, tree progress and active secret bonuses. [§ HUD, dashboard and settings](../../../BIBLE.md#hud-dashboard-and-settings): line 594 names the four labeled slot cells of the HUD mockup, line 596 requires the dashboard to distinguish locked slot, unavailable upgrade, permitted equipment swap and special tree respec, and line 602 names sensitivity, sound, UI scale and impact shake as settings. [§ 5.5 What a discovery changes](../../../BIBLE.md#55-what-a-discovery-changes): line 460 separates acquired from equipped, line 461 makes a branch change require a special respec opportunity, line 462 keeps recipe knowledge while its bonus needs the eligible current-run build again, line 463 makes a permanent unlock persist without accumulating permanent combat-stat advantage, and line 465 forbids duplicating rewards, refilling a spent revival or adding another copy of a recipe effect on load.
 - [docs/project/DECISION-REGISTER.md](../../../docs/project/DECISION-REGISTER.md) rows D26 and D27, lines 49 and 50. D26 leaves when permanent discoveries are written open, preserves discoveries on defeat, settles results once and adopts no concrete storage or write schedule. D27 leaves the run-checkpoint schema and permanent-profile compatibility to be specified after run state is defined, supersedes the old v2 sketch as a concrete contract and implies no migration or baseline-profile retirement. Both are Open. This section therefore names fields and types without adopting a write schedule, a migration plan or a retirement policy; the write schedule is [Q-E09](../../../BACKLOG.md#q-e09) and the commit-boundary card's, and migration is [HF-09](../../../BACKLOG.md#hf-09) (Specify schema and gameplay-content migration).
-- [HF-06b](HF-06b-persistence-projection.md) revision 1 (Map matrix rows to persistence projections), section bytes SHA256 `bbd5edb186636bafea1b7ba9d75bbf9ceb3d7ab1cf5d23a6e32c95154d8aadf9` and [CSV](HF-06b-persistence-projection.csv) bytes SHA256 `e4f23fc334277fe41ed05eef71b136b050d9163c83e616010afce62326413783` at this base. Its fourteen `json-projection` rows and the projection-group vocabulary at its lines 55 to 71 are the fields this section places. Its line 34 rule 4 makes every projected ID a JSON string and hands the numeric typing of counters and generations to this section. Its line 63 reserves a `checkpoint.device-carry-over` group whose field set may be empty. Its line 77 records why the Q-P15 rows hold under every answer, and its line 81 records that the Q-P16 interruption rule could add a checkpoint field that would be this section's and the commit-boundary card's.
+- [HF-06b](HF-06b-persistence-projection.md) revision 1 (Map matrix rows to persistence projections), section bytes SHA256 `83f6e4ba248518d1979e1428ace02ec99fea202722ab6aa0bab531f766094014` and [CSV](HF-06b-persistence-projection.csv) bytes SHA256 `b42918083688be02511496932e20db19305e7407dc785d740b4e0fedf6779a48` at this base. Its fourteen `json-projection` rows and the projection-group vocabulary at its lines 55 to 71 are the fields this section places. Its line 34 rule 4 makes every projected ID a JSON string and hands the numeric typing of counters and generations to this section. Its line 63 reserves a `checkpoint.device-carry-over` group whose field set may be empty. Its line 77 records why the Q-P15 rows hold under every answer, and its line 81 records that the Q-P16 interruption rule could add a checkpoint field that would be this section's and the commit-boundary card's.
 - [HF-03a](HF-03a-module-map.md) revision 1, section bytes SHA256 `95fbd03d067fd0da2d122130ae3c54284116adc92f40c7f69c91946fd941e4cc` at this base. Line 35 of its module table gives Persistence the owned mutable records `SaveTransactionState`, `DurableAggregate`, `PreferencesRecord` and `RecoveryState`. Line 49 makes `SaveTransactionState` hold the candidate aggregate, the transaction and generation identity and commit status, makes `DurableAggregate` the validated last committed JSON projection of profile, checkpoint and lifecycle facts in storage separate from Session's live records, makes `PreferencesRecord` the separately versioned preferences data, and reserves staging, replacement and file writes to Persistence alone while Session alone installs a loaded value into fresh live records. Line 45 places the live `RunState` and `ProfileState` in Session. Line 58 makes a durable spent-revival or terminal fact take precedence over an older checkpoint during restore. Line 96 records that Q-E09 gates which discoveries commit immediately and that no live ProfileState mutation implies an invented retention policy.
 - [HF-05](HF-05-content-admission.md) revision 2. Line 18 defines the domain ID as an opaque, nonempty, case-sensitive token compared exactly. Line 23 defines the gameplay content revision and states that its token has no assumed numeric ordering. Line 27 requires a saved pair of gameplay content revision and domain ID to resolve to one gameplay meaning and never through an unqualified latest catalogue. Line 54 defines a current tree selection as a connected unlocked prefix and requires loaded selections to be validated again at the Session and Persistence boundary. Line 56 rebuilds `EffectiveBuild` from current equipped selections and selected tree paths and stops a removed item from contributing. Line 58 preserves actual offered choices and resolved rewards without rerolling.
