e that a profile entry commits only at the next durable transition. Lines 129 to 135 are the nonduplication invariants N1 to N7, N5 now reading for both outcomes and for the one transition that changes `run.run_id`. Line 143 carries the interruption and revival policies with [Q-P16](../../../BACKLOG.md#q-p16) resolved at TRACKING EV-0247, P1 adopted with R2 and the rest retained as history, and line 155 fixes when a non-null `run.interruption` would commit and records that under P1 nothing does. Line 173 decides that acknowledgement leaves no durable trace, so a crash between commit and acknowledge is indistinguishable on storage from a crash after acknowledge. Line 175 decides that a preferences write uses the same four stages over its own document, carries no `generation` and no `transaction_id`, has no place in `A`, and is **not** a critical write under TADR-004 line 32; this section owns the failure-handling half of that decision. Line 306 deliberately leaves the qualified filesystem protocol unchosen and hands write ordering, flush and commit behaviour, recovery evidence and single-writer ownership per target OS to this card. Line 307 hands this card a preserved candidate, an ambiguous lifecycle record, a corrupt record and an unsupported newer record. Line 309 records that no numeric threshold is set there; none is set here either.
