 ### Carried state and its owner
 
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@ Sources: BIBLE lines 475, 519, 578, 580, 582 and 584; docs/DISCOVERY.md line 11.
 
 **Rebuilt-each-run power.** Within a run the player builds combat power; at run end that power resets and the discoveries do not. Every character has four character-specific binary trees, each a root that forks twice again to eight endpoints, with one connected root-to-endpoint lineage selected per slot (BIBLE line 529). The weapon slot and special mobility are available at run start; the main hero skill and the ultimate unlock through play during world one (BIBLE lines 533 to 536). A normal successful route reaches an endpoint in every tree by the final boss, and elapsed time is not the gate (BIBLE lines 515, 538). `EffectiveBuild` is derived and never durable: it is rebuilt from current selections and admitted definitions whenever a selection changes, so removed equipment stops contributing and repeated swaps accumulate nothing (HF-03a lines 45, 57; TADR-002 line 32; BIBLE line 552). At RL9 the next run rebuilds equipment power, tree progress and active secret bonuses, and no permanent combat-stat advantage accumulates (BIBLE lines 463, 475, 586). Node effects, costs and milestone allocation are Q-P11 and Q-P10; inventory capacity and equipped limits are Q-P19; the respec opportunity is Q-P18; companion assembly and device lifecycle are Q-P15; recipe eligibility is Q-P14. None is chosen here.
 
-**Permanent discoveries.** Permanent discoveries, learned recipes, options and challenges survive defeat (BIBLE line 586; docs/DISCOVERY.md line 33). In the durable record they are sets that only grow: a repeated commit adds no second copy and grants no bonus, because the bonus is rebuilt rather than stored (HF-07b line 135). A discovered recipe's effect still requires the eligible current-run build again, and respeccing out of the combination removes the derived bonus while retaining the knowledge (BIBLE lines 562, 564). Transition D validates that the three profile sets are supersets of the committed ones, which is how the loop's terminal state preserves them (HF-07b line 108). Which facts create a discovery is Q-P37; when a discovery fact commits is Q-E09, whose product half is unanswered and whose two poles both use the same four stages and the same N7 invariant (HF-07b line 305).
